'' A CONSTANT'S DECLARED TYPE IS PART OF ITS VALUE, and nothing was reading it.
''
'' 'const v as ubyte = not u' folded to the INITIALISER's value and stopped there, so
'' v was -1 where fbc has 255 -- and it lowered and verified, as an i8 holding the
'' wrong number. Measured: fbc's C for 'dim as longint x = v' is 'X = 255ll'.
''
'' The string fold had the other half of it: ConstStringTextOf_ passed no scope, so a
'' NAMED constant argument was looked up in scope 0 and never found. 'str( 5 )' folded
'' and 'str( b )' did not, which is why this looked fine -- and it is every USE of the
'' resulting constant that declined, never a line mentioning str.
'' numbers/const_op.bas is 8 of them.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/const-declared-width.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-OUT: const i8 255
'' EXPECT-OUT: const i16 65535
'' EXPECT-OUT: const i32 4294967295
'' EXPECT-OUT: "255"
'' GOLDEN: expected/const-declared-width.out
